 "notes": "Four-rod RF quadrupole built entirely from analytic circle shapes \u2014 no STL files. Rod radius 4.408 mm at r0 = 3.84 mm (rod/r0 = 1.148, the classic cylindrical approximation); RF 241.34 V zero-to-peak at 2.0 MHz puts m/z 100 at q = 0.40 (stable) and m/z 30 at q = 1.33 (unstable). Both masses are flown together: the stable mass oscillates bounded for the whole flight while the unstable mass grows and strikes a rod or the ejection window \u2014 the Mathieu stability demonstration in one flight. Same electrical design as the STL-rod transport example, so the two can be compared route-for-route.",
